# Backend Library API — Ground Truth

Created: 2026-02-04 08:55 UTC  
Last reviewed: 2026-02-04 08:55 UTC

## Purpose
Expose the Postgres-backed `library_item` table via FastAPI so the frontend `Library` tab can load real data.

## Files
- Models/schemas: `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/models.py`
- Routes: `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/api/routes/library.py`
- Router wiring: `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/api/main.py`

## Endpoints
- `GET /api/v1/library/` (auth required)
  - Query params: `workflow_key`, `kind`, `q`, `current_only=true`, `skip`, `limit`
  - `q` uses `ILIKE` on `title` or `body_mdc`
  - `current_only` filters `superseded_by_id is null`
- `GET /api/v1/library/workflow-keys` (auth required)
  - Returns distinct `workflow_key` values with counts (for "bucket" grouping UI)
  - `current_only=true` counts only current (non-superseded) items
- `GET /api/v1/library/{id}` (auth required)
- `POST /api/v1/library/` (superuser required)
- `PUT /api/v1/library/{id}` (superuser required)
  - Update is implemented as **supersede**: creates a new row and sets `superseded_by_id` on the old row

## Notes
- Deletes are intentionally not implemented; supersede is the supported evolution mechanism.
